\ LISTSET.SEQ   Allow adjusting the LIST segment of F-PC   F-PC native port

\ Assure #LISTSEGS has at least "segments" of free memory and then
\ re-save F-PC back to disk where it came from with the same name if
\ we needed to change the segments available.

\ F-PC native port: list space is a fixed region of the VM's flat memory
\ (it ends at LIST-LIMIT), not a DOS segment whose size is saved in the
\ .EXE, so there is nothing to adjust and nothing to re-save. LISTSET
\ only reports whether the free list space covers the request
\ ("segments" are still 16 byte paragraphs) and then leaves, as before.
\ #LISTSEGS is kept as a plain VALUE so old scripts that set it with =:
\ (F-PC.SEQ does) still load; its value means nothing natively.

\- #listsegs    0 value #listsegs       \ unused natively, see above

: LISTSET       ( segments -- )
                16 *  LIST-LIMIT XHERE -        ( bytes-wanted bytes-free )
                cr ." LIST space is fixed in this F-PC, "
                dup u. ." bytes are free."
                u>
        if      cr ." That is less than requested, and it can't be changed."
        else    cr ." No save needed, listseg correct."
        then    cr bye ;
